							},
							{
								"box": {
									"code": "// State pix (f_tf_smooth): the temporal one-pole recurrence, per channel, in\n// tensor space. in1 = this frame's raw tensor (f_tensor_type.md outlet-0\n// encoding, unchanged by smoothing); in2 = previous frame's blended output\n// (feedback loop, see codebox_render.gen + definition.py pix_wires).\n// Mirrors tests/test_tf_smooth.py smooth_step exactly.\n//\n//   T' = T_new + release * (T_prev - T_new)\n//\n// ADR-3: NO clamp anywhere. Raw tensor values are unbounded floats (strong\n// edges give Jxx*strength >> 1); clipping inside a feedback loop creates\n// stuck-at-boundary artifacts. The outlet encoding IS the inlet encoding\n// (raw tensor passthrough), so this module never encodes or clamps at all.\n// No decode, no atan2: this codebox is 4-channel arithmetic only.\n//\n// ADR-4: bypass_gate (module bypass, bypass_mode \"param\"; NOT the native\n// @bypass, which would skip the shader and flip feedback semantics) is an\n// exact passthrough with the feedback IGNORED -- not a freeze of the last\n// smoothed frame. On an unconnected inlet (vs_black = zero tensor) the\n// feedback decays naturally to the zero-tensor neutral instead of holding a\n// stale field.\n//\n// GATE PROVISIONAL-OPEN (spec OQ1 / tasks T016): release default 0.5 and the\n// dial ceiling are PROVISIONAL, pending tier-3 judgement on live noise.\n// The shipped literal follows definition.py's declared default (0.5).\nParam release(0.5);\nParam bypass_gate(0.0);\n\nnew_t = sample(in1, norm);            // inline access (stored-variable .x silent-fails)\nprev_t = sample(in2, norm);\n\n// Per-channel one-pole. mix(a, b, w) = a + w*(b - a): blend(prev, new, 1-release)\n// = new + release*(prev - new) with no float32 reorder surprises.\nout1 = mix(prev_t, new_t, -release + 1.0);\n// ADR-4 bypass: passthrough of the inlet, feedback ignored.\nout1 = mix(out1, new_t, bypass_gate);",
									"fontface": 0,
									"fontname": "<Monospaced>",
									"fontsize": 12.0,
									"id": "gen-obj-2",
									"maxclass": "codebox",
									"numinlets": 2,
									"numoutlets": 1,
									"outlettype": [
										""
									],
									"patching_rect": [
										22.0,
										80.0,
										550.0,
										380.0
									]
								}
							},
